README.OSK -- how this tree differs from 4.3BSD-Net/2's usr/src/games/arithmeticORIG/ is the tree exactly as Net/2 carried it: arithmetic, Eamonn McManus'sdrill in sums (Trinity College Dublin), in the University of California's1991 release.  obj (a symlink into the build machine) and tags are notcarried.The program itself is unchanged.  Under -DOSK:  arithmetic.c  <signal.h> and <time.h> in place of <sys/signal.h>; BSD's                random(), srandom() and index() are the C library's rand(),                srand() and strchr().  And when a read fails it calls                unix.l's check_signal() first: on OS-9 the interrupt aborts                the read, and that library's signal() only records the                signal, so without the call ^C left with no score -- now                intr() prints it, as it did under BSD.  getopt.c      Henry Spencer's public-domain getopt, which this C library                lacks, as SRC/wump carries it.